  "howToPlay": {
    "json": {
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "How to Play\n\nPowerball\u00ae jackpots start at $20 million. There are 9 ways to win and if you match the first 5 numbers with Power Play\u00ae, you are guaranteed a $2 million cash prize! You may also have a second chance to win each night if you purchase the Double Play\u00ae option.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "You can purchase Powerball tickets online any time by selecting the Buy Now button and adding tickets to your shopping cart. When making your purchase online, you can select Quick Pick to have numbers automatically selected for you, choose Create My Own Ticket to select your own lucky numbers, play Same As Last Time to recreate your last ticket, or select Subscribe so you never miss a draw.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "To purchase tickets at retail, ask the store clerk for a Quick Pick (QP) ticket or fill out a play slip. Each play slip has five boards.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "Each Powerball play costs $2 and numbers are drawn from two sets of numbers: one set from 1 through 69 and the second set from 1 through 26.",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "To play, pick five numbers from the set of 69 numbers, and one number (the Powerball number) from the set of 26 numbers. When creating your own ticket online or using a play slip at retail, fill in or select the squares from the numbers you wish to play. If using a play slip at retail, do not used red ink or erase. If you make an error on the retail play slip mark the VOID square, and them make selections on another board. ",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "If you want to play the Power Play, mark the Power Play square. The Power Play number will be selected before each Powerball draw and depending upon the number selected, your non-jackpot prize winnings will be multiplied by 2, 3, 4, 5, or 10, except the $1 million dollar prize that will be doubled. The Power Play costs an additional $1 per board played.",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "If you want to play the Double Play, mark the Double Play square. Choosing Double Play costs an additional $1 per board played on the play slip. The Double Play drawing will be held after the scheduled Powerball drawing and offers an additional chance to win on your original numbers by matching a new set of numbers drawn.",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "To have the terminal randomly pick the numbers for you at retail, either mark the QP option on the play slip for up to five boards and your desired multi-draw option or ask the stork clerk for a QP ticket for up to five boards and your desired multi-draw option ($2 per board played, plus an additional $1 for Power Play if selected and an additional $1 for Double Play if selected).",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "Both Power Play and Double Play features can be selected for the Powerball ticket, however, the Power Play multiplier does not apply to the prizes won in the Double Play drawing.",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "ordered-list"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "* The 10X multiplier will only be used when the advertised annuitized jackpot is $150 million or less.\n\n** The Match 5 prize will NOT be multiplied and will remain at $2 million for a Match 5+0 win when the Power Play option is purchased as an add-on to the Powerball play. The Jackpot prize is not included in the Power Play multiplier option.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
